                               DMITop v1.0a.
                            ------------------

WHAT IS DMITOP?
---------------

 Well, nothing more than the ordinary TopTen-user-list generating tool,
 that already exists. All it does is to scan your accounts, collecting 
 the data for the different toplists (6 of'em in fact), sorting it out,
 and write it all down to it's specific place. 


WHAT SHOULD BE IN THE ARCHIVE?
------------------------------

 In the archive you should have the following files:

   DMITop.REXX				-The TopTen-program
   DMITop.DOC				-The file you reading now
   QSort				-A very good sort program
   QSort.readme				-The extremly short doc's for QSort

 If some of the files missing, then call the person from whom you got it,
 and demand the rest of the files (actually, you only need Qsort & the 
 DMITop.REXX-file). And of course, your board should be running on CNet 2.60
 or greater for this to work.


HOW TO INSTALL:
---------------

 Fairly simple actually, Install the DMITop.REXX anywhere in your PFILES:
 directory, and add it to your pfile-list as an ordinary AREXX-file. Then
 go to your GFILES: directory and add a subboard to the list with the path
 'GFILES:DMITop'. The load you're favourite editor, and open the DMITop.REXX
 file and edit the following two lines #20,#20, which would look like this:

  startacc=2

 Change the '2' to the starting account you wish to have, Starting on 2, 
 skip the SysOp-account, a '3' will skip the account after that and so on...

 The next line is:

  endacc=100

 This is the final account that will be scanned when running this file.
 It could be any number actually, just make sure that it's higher than 
 the final accountnumber (i.e if you got 140 users, set endacc=200) and
 you can be sure to have all you're users counted for.

 The Lastthing to do is to copy the QSort file to your C: directory, and
 then DMITop well be ready to run.

WHAT'S NEW?
-----------

	v1.0  :  The absolute first version of DMITop
	v1.0a :  Added the 'Updated on' option


